INT. JUNO'S BEDROOM - NIGHT

Dark. Fairy lights, half of them dead.

Posters. A beanbag. Laundry in a heap that could be anything.

JUNO (16) lies in bed, earbuds out, eyes open. She listens.

Silence.

Then, through the wall: a thud. A slow one.

She sits up.

Another thud. Wood on wood.

She grabs her phone. Taps it. Nothing. Her phone. Dead.

The thudding finds a rhythm. Four beats. Four beats. Under it, a low hum, wrong, like something breathing through a tube.

JUNO
(whisper)
Hello?

Nothing.

She swings her legs out. Floorboard creaks. She freezes. Waits.

The wall goes quiet.

Then a voice, muffled, lazy, sung half a note flat.

THE BAND (O.S.)
(muffled, through wall)
Wonderwall... one, two, three...

Juno stares at the wall.

THE BAND (O.S.) (CONT'D)
(muffled)
Sorry! Sorry! Dave, you're on the wrong key!

A cymbal CRASHES. A guitar squeals.

Juno exhales. Her whole body unclenches. She laughs, a short, shaky bark.

JUNO
(to the wall)
It's one a.m.!

THE BAND (O.S.)
(muffled)
Sorry, Juno!

A pause. She lies back. Pulls the duvet up.

Quiet.

Rain on the window.

Her closet door, which was closed, is open now. An inch.

She doesn't see it. She closes her eyes.

From the wall, soft, in unison:

THE BAND (O.S.)
(muffled, hushed)
...we're not in the garage, Juno.

Her eyes snap open.

Silence.
